From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: George Whewell <georgerw@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 19:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 0062] media: sophgo: cap SG2002 CSI capture buffer count

The SG2002 boards give CSI capture and Coda980 a 32 MiB shared coherent
pool.  A 2560x1440 packed RAW10 buffer is 5.5 MiB, but the reserved-memory
allocator rounds it to an 8 MiB order-11 allocation.  Capture also needs an
8 MiB scratch buffer at STREAMON.  A conventional client requesting four
MMAP buffers therefore consumes the complete pool before STREAMON and the
scratch allocation fails with -ENOMEM, even when ordinary RAM and CMA are
otherwise free.

The DMA engine only needs two capture buffers: one active and one queued,
with scratch absorbing userspace starvation.  Limit the queue to that
proven budget.  Account for buffers already present so CREATE_BUFS cannot
grow the queue past the same limit.  Do this in queue_setup rather than
vb2_queue.max_num_buffers, since this kernel rejects values below
VB2_MAX_FRAME during queue initialization.

Signed-off-by: George Whewell <georgerw@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/sophgo/sg2002-capture.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/sophgo/sg2002-capture.c b/drivers/media/platform/sophgo/sg2002-capture.c
index 2f72a55d1..ec2b4e042 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/sophgo/sg2002-capture.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/sophgo/sg2002-capture.c
@@ -44,6 +44,7 @@
 #define SG2002_HEIGHT		1080
 #define SG2002_BYTES_PER_LINE	ALIGN(SG2002_WIDTH * 2, 16)
 #define SG2002_SIZE_IMAGE	(SG2002_BYTES_PER_LINE * SG2002_HEIGHT)
+#define SG2002_CAPTURE_MAX_BUFFERS	2
 
 /* CSI MAC0 register blocks. */
 #define MAC_TOP_CTRL		0x000
@@ -880,7 +881,14 @@ static int sg2002_queue_setup(struct vb2_queue *q, unsigned int *num_buffers,
 			      struct device *alloc_devs[])
 {
 	struct sg2002_capture *cap = vb2_get_drv_priv(q);
+	unsigned int allocated = vb2_get_num_buffers(q);
 
+	/* The private media pool budgets two frame buffers plus scratch. */
+	if (allocated >= SG2002_CAPTURE_MAX_BUFFERS)
+		return -ENOBUFS;
+	*num_buffers = min(*num_buffers,
+			   SG2002_CAPTURE_MAX_BUFFERS - allocated);
+
 	if (*num_planes)
 		return sizes[0] < cap->sizeimage ? -EINVAL : 0;
 
